      "lineNbr": 25,
      "author": {
        "id": 1843125
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-05-19T17:06:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e A comment that explains this part would be helpful.  It\u0027s related to having to build multiple __init functions into the fips140.ko module, right?\n\nYes.\n\n\u003e How is it guaranteed that they are run in the right order?\n\nThey are executed in ascending initcall level order, just like they are when they are built into vmlinux. This is due to the fact that all crypto objects are gathered into a pair of .a files that are built as built-ins, which are linked into the fips140.ko module.",
      "parentUuid": "14696213_b856d571",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "7284f0af63f3973eef9d971b00c7f5ef37d50428",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
