      "writtenOn": "2021-05-19T17:12:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I am worried about the data structures not matching between GKI and the FIPS module.\n\nNormally, GKI has to maintain a stable ABI for modules.\n\nIs that not something we have to worry about here because the FIPS module will be built and distributed alongside GKI, instead of being built and distributed alongside device modules (which could be much older than the GKI they are used with)?",
